{"orgCode":"0390","name":"Contributions to the Judges' Retirement System","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The Judges' Retirement System provides retirement benefit funding for judges on California's Supreme, Appellate, and Superior/Municipal courts. The California Public Employees' Retirement System administers both the Judges' Retirement System and the Judges' Retirement System II on behalf of its members.\n\nThe Judges' Retirement System is closed to new members, and a second retirement system for judges was established in 1994. All new judges elected or appointed on or after November 9, 1994 become members of the Judges' Retirement System II. The Judges' Retirement System II provides retirement, disability, and death benefits based on age, years of service, final compensation, and eligibility, as determined by specific sections of the Judges' Retirement System II Law. Judges' Retirement System II members eligible for a service retirement have the option of choosing the monetary credit plan (a lump-sum return of contributions and interest earned) or the defined benefit plan. Judges' Retirement System II members not eligible for a defined benefit receive the balance of their monetary credits (in a lump-sum payment). The Judges' Retirement System II is funded through contributions from the state, members of the system, and investment earnings. The state's contributions are adjusted annually to maintain actuarial soundness of the fund.\n\nThe Judges' Retirement System provides retirement, disability, and death benefits based on age, years of service, compensation of active judges, and eligibility, as determined by specific sections of the Judges' Retirement Law. Active judges and the state each contribute 8 percent of salary to the Judges' Retirement System. Additional contributions come from filing fees for specific civil cases and investment income. These contributions, however, are not sufficient to fully fund benefit payments. Consequently, current law requires the state to fund the difference between existing contribution sources and the required benefit payments to retired judges.\n\nEffective January 1, 2013, provisions of the California Public Employees' Pension Reform Act of 2013, Chapter 296, Statutes of 2012 (AB 340), require that new judges contribute 50 percent of the normal cost of their pension benefits.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":318500,"cy":282468,"by":306104},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":317670,"cy":317601,"by":322967}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0390","kind":"department","name":"Contributions to the Judges' Retirement System","code":"0390","amounts":{"py":318500,"cy":282468,"by":306104},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":318500,"cy":282468,"by":306104}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0390/0190","kind":"program","name":"State Operations","code":"0190","amounts":{"py":6608,"cy":6501,"by":6223},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":6608,"cy":6501,"by":6223}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":6608,"cy":6501,"by":6223}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0390/0190/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":6608,"cy":6501,"by":6223},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":6608,"cy":6501,"by":6223}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":6608,"cy":6501,"by":6223}}}}]},{"id":"exp/0010/0390/0195","kind":"program","name":"Local Assistance","code":"0195","amounts":{"py":311892,"cy":275967,"by":299881},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":311892,"cy":275967,"by":299881}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":311892,"cy":275967,"by":299881}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0390/0195/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":311892,"cy":275967,"by":299881},"byFundType":{"general":{"